Upgrade procedure for less

Source: https://greenwoodsoftware.com/less/less-VERSION.tar.gz

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and extract the official less-VERSION.tar.gz release archive.
2. Import it on vendor/less/dist, retaining the complete upstream release.
3. Merge it into master with:

       git subtree merge -P contrib/less vendor/less/dist

4. Keep the master-only files and compatibility changes described below.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - 886d52f19ea3e264811d0a93fce22af07fc0e6aa: Apply less is more
    patches from FreeBSD.  Preserve less-is-more behavior in command.c,
    forwback.c, main.c, pattern.h, and signal.c.  The patches are applied
    around command-mode search modifiers, forward-screen handling, option
    parsing and terminal initialization, POSIX regular expressions, and
    interrupt handling.

  - 0828cc62cd5d05bba93fb2ea29c35922e7febd9f: Port the less-is-more
    changes to less 704.  In less.h, retain the HAVE_WCTYPE_H guard and
    wctype.h include; HAVE_WCTYPE is enabled by usr.bin/less/defines.h.

Notes:

  - master excludes upstream configuration files, non-Unix makefiles,
    generated manual pages, install helpers, and the lesstest directory.
    Keep those exclusions after each subtree merge.
  - Use the Less License included in LICENSE; COPYING is intentionally
    excluded from the master subtree.
